{"body":"**Admin access counts are wrong, and the footnote asserts the opposite.** `GET /suites` runs with `include_all=is_workspace_admin(current_user)` and `effective_permissions` stamps every non-owned suite `admin` (`suite_authz.py:66-67`). So for a workspace admin, "Shared with you as admin" is *every suite in the workspace nobody shared*, while this line says those suites "are not counted here". A fresh admin in a 40-suite workspace reads "Shared with you as admin: 40" when no one shared anything. The payload cannot distinguish an explicit `admin` share from the role-derived stamp, so either drop the per-level counts for admins (show "you can act on all N suites") or have the API expose the grant source.

